1
00:00:01,730 --> 00:00:03,230
Kou?

2
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:05,440
Yuuri?

3
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:08,440
Oh, there you are.

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,650
What happened? I thought you'd be right back.

5
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,820
Also, where's Yuuri?

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,790
Don't worry about it.

7
00:00:29,710 --> 00:00:32,840
Did something happen with Kou?

8
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:43,350
Nothing at all.

9
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:48,270
Whatever it is,

10
00:00:49,190 --> 00:00:51,400
it's not "nothing at all".

11
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:57,200
The world has fallen in love

12
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,870
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

13
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:04,160
I just want to understand you

14
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:08,540
Won't you open up to me?

15
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:19,680
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

16
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:23,020
Enough to make me cry

17
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:28,350
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

18
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:35,490
and put it all in tune

19
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:41,330
I lost sight of everything but my goal

20
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:45,000
and had something important fade away

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,250
Let's start all over

22
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:56,380
The world has fallen in love

23
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:59,640
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

24
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:03,220
I want to know everything about you

25
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:07,390
Won't you tell me more?

26
00:02:07,390 --> 00:02:11,020
One inch feels like a million miles

27
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:13,940
as the days just seem to race by

28
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:18,360
I won't and can't ever forget

29
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:21,620
this brightest page of my life.

30
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:32,420
Oh, you got it right. This one too.

31
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:37,800
Kou and Yuuri...

32
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:40,550
What were they doing down there?

33
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:42,890
Chemistry

34
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:42,890
Easy to understand

35
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:49,520
She averted her eyes again!

36
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:53,190
What was it? What happened?!

37
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:55,650
Did one of them confess or something?

38
00:02:53,190 --> 00:03:02,160
Check
your answers!

39
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:59,320
Or maybe they even k...

40
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:02,160
No, stop! Stop thinking about that!

41
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:04,160
I'm a wreck.

42
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:08,250
By the way, how'd you solve this one?

43
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,330
The way you just told me to.

44
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:14,790
Could Kou... like Yuuri back?

45
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:19,630
Are you kidding me, Kou?
You got it down pat right away.

46
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:22,930
Do you just not pay attention in class?

47
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,680
Why do you hate studying so much?

48
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:29,640
It's not so much that I hate it,

49
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,940
I just feel like it's pointless.

50
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:35,820
That's right.

51
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:39,780
I must be an idiot for doing something so pointless.

52
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,860
How stupid.

53
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,030
Don't say that!

54
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:47,830
If you don't keep up with your studies now,

55
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:50,330
you really will be held back!

56
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,500
I don't want that to happen!

57
00:03:53,170 --> 00:03:56,290
Nobody would be happy to see that!

58
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:58,380
Yuuri...

59
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:07,310
Why?

60
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,770
What's this tension between them?

61
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:14,230
Makita, I didn't know you had such a fire in you!

62
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:17,940
You're totally right! We all need to move up together.

63
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,530
Besides, if you screw up another set of finals,

64
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,200
you'll be spending your whole summer doing make-up classes.

65
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:27,330
Then we wouldn't be able to all hang out together.

66
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:30,660
Yeah, we should make plans together.

67
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,330
Could you maybe ask me first?

68
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:37,630
Let's see... any day except Obon works for me.

69
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:42,470
Hear that? Let's put in a bit more effort, huh?

70
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,600
Sure.

71
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,440
But I'm too tired for more today.

72
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:56,980
Sorry.

73
00:05:02,990 --> 00:05:06,360
After all's said and done, we did pretty well.

74
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,450
You're right about that.

75
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:14,120
What really surprised me though was when Yuuri got so passionate.

76
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,960
I guess something really did happen with Kou then?

77
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,590
That hesitation...

78
00:05:25,590 --> 00:05:27,340
Nothing at all.

79
00:05:31,350 --> 00:05:35,060
...says that it's something she doesn't want me to know.

80
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:43,690
Saketani Station

81
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:40,730
See ya!

82
00:05:40,730 --> 00:05:42,020
Good work all around.

83
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,690
Bye-bye, Futaba-chan!

84
00:05:43,690 --> 00:05:44,690
Bye-bye.

85
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:58,080
I can't let this go!

86
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:08,090
Oh, Kou. Sorry... huh?

87
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:12,100
Were you going somewhere? Sorry.

88
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:15,890
Not yet. I've still got a bit of time.

89
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:17,600
What's up?

90
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:22,110
A-Actually...

91
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:27,360
I think I forgot my cellphone.

92
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:30,740
What, really? Wonder if it's in my room.

93
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,030
I'll try calling it.

94
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:35,040
Come help look.

95
00:06:41,290 --> 00:06:43,500
Mind if I use your bathroom?

96
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,380
Can I get a cup of water?

97
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,430
I can't find the right timing.

98
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:54,890
7th cup

99
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:58,310
So? What did you really come here for?

100
00:06:58,810 --> 00:07:01,310
You've entertained me enough by now.

101
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:02,980
So he knew...

102
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:02,980
bulge

103
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:10,030
Well, Kou...

104
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,700
Did something happen with Yuuri?

105
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,290
Nothing worth talking about.

106
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:23,040
The same hesitation as Yuuri.

107
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:25,960
This isn't fair.

108
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,510
Why won't you tell me?

109
00:07:30,930 --> 00:07:34,930
I just noticed Yuuri was acting strange.

110
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:39,020
But Yuuri said nothing happened either...

111
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:43,850
If Makita said it was nothing,
then why not believe her?

112
00:07:44,310 --> 00:07:46,480
It's not something you should worry about.

113
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:50,280
I'm the only one being left out.

114
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:52,410
There's nothing left to say.

115
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:54,780
I doubt that.

116
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,910
There's also one more thing.

117
00:07:58,790 --> 00:08:03,000
I want to know... why you changed.

118
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:08,920
What, that again?

119
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:13,590
I thought I told you to stop looking for my past self.

120
00:08:15,010 --> 00:08:16,720
I'm not looking.

121
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:19,560
I'm through with looking for who you used to be.

122
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,440
I want to know who you are right now.

123
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:26,610
I want to know everything you went though.

124
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:34,570
You know,

125
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:38,740
when someone keeps dodging their questions,

126
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:41,200
most people don't probe any further.

127
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,170
You're pretty incredible.

128
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:46,000
I see what he's doing.

129
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,460
He's trying to sarcasm his way out of this.

130
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,960
But that won't stop me!

131
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:57,510
Fine.

132
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,680
Wait, Kou?

133
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,900
What'd you do that...

134
00:09:17,070 --> 00:09:18,620
My mother.

135
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:22,330
Don't give me that face.

136
00:09:22,910 --> 00:09:26,000
I wasn't trying to hide it or anything.

137
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:30,340
Though even if you knew, I'm not sure you'd be able to say much.

138
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,800
Besides, I knew

139
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:35,380
that you would react like this.

140
00:09:38,890 --> 00:09:39,890
Makita, too.

141
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:44,060
She reacted the exact same way you did.

142
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:55,400
When Yuuri found out about Kou's mom

143
00:09:57,110 --> 00:10:01,910
she must've found it impossible to talk about.

144
00:10:01,910 --> 00:10:03,450
Nothing at all.

145
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,830
And here I am...

146
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:13,130
...doubting every little thing about them.

147
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:20,970
Sorry.

148
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:23,310
Why are you apologizing?

149
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:26,850
Both Kou and Yuuri

150
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:31,730
were trying to be sensitive to other people's feelings.

151
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:39,200
But all I think about is myself.

152
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:42,320
You're such a crybaby.

153
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:44,370
Okay, that's enough.

154
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,620
Sorry.

155
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,260
You don't know when to quit.

156
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:15,110
You won't... drop out, right?

157
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:26,830
Kou, don't you want to be with us?

158
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,540
Because I...

159
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:36,800
...I want to be with you!

160
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,600
H-Hey, stop that...

161
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,270
You've got the wrong idea.

162
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:37,190
I told her about Mom and she started crying.

163
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,490
I see.

164
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,410
Whoops, I need to get going.

165
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,880
Where are you going? Don't tell me...

166
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,710
I've got work today.

167
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:00,880
Work?

168
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:06,390
What, today's a work day?
Want me to give you a ride?

169
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:07,550
I'm fine.

170
00:13:09,810 --> 00:13:11,430
Take her home instead.

171
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:15,850
W-Wait...

172
00:13:35,750 --> 00:13:37,880
What am I doing?

173
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:46,510
Tanaka-sensei, are you on bad terms with Kou?

174
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:57,770
Kou probably can't forgive me.

175
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,520
It started when our parents divorced.

176
00:14:03,690 --> 00:14:07,030
Kou, I'll leave Mom in your hands.

177
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,110
Got it.

178
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:21,250
As I said that, I left all the hard work to Kou

179
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,590
when we needed each other the most.

180
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:30,840
Right turn here?

181
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:31,970
Yes.

182
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:47,030
When our mother fell ill and was admitted to the hospital,

183
00:14:47,570 --> 00:14:52,910
Tanaka Youichi

184
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:55,450
I had just started my teaching job.

185
00:14:56,870 --> 00:15:03,170
I couldn't visit the hospital she was
transferred to in Nagasaki very often.

186
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:24,270
It pained me to see my mother growing thinner every time I saw her.

187
00:15:21,270 --> 00:15:25,230
Mabuchi

188
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:33,530
I was always scared to step inside her room.

189
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:38,000
Really, really scared.

190
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:42,620
But I left him alone

191
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:47,250
to experience that day after day.

192
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:58,140
Kou's actually a really nice and kind boy. That's why—

193
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,310
I know.

194
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,900
I know.

195
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,700
Isn't he?

196
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:17,740
He's a good kid.

197
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,080
Thank you.

198
00:16:36,970 --> 00:16:42,730
The more things you view as precious, the more they weigh you down.

199
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:51,690
Those were the words of someone who knows the fear of loss.

200
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:59,240
That's why Kou became the person he is.

201
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,410
Kou.

202
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:15,550
You've been walking through a night

203
00:17:17,470 --> 00:17:18,970
I didn't know about.

204
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,690
That's why...

205
00:17:29,770 --> 00:17:32,230
But I'm too tired for more today.

206
00:17:32,230 --> 00:17:33,150
Sorry.

207
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:34,860
I'm fine.

208
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:36,860
Take her home instead.

209
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,620
W-Wait...

210
00:17:43,290 --> 00:17:44,370
But Kou,

211
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:49,500
I know that's not all.

212
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:54,510
No matter how abrasive or blunt you may act,

213
00:17:56,090 --> 00:18:01,720
I know that down inside, you're kind.

214
00:18:10,270 --> 00:18:11,360
Sorry.

215
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:17,490
Futaba-chan, what happened?

216
00:18:17,490 --> 00:18:19,530
Why are you apologizing?

217
00:18:21,370 --> 00:18:25,580
I made Kou tell me about his mother.

218
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:31,840
You didn't know whether it was alright to tell me,

219
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:34,420
so you said it was nothing.

220
00:18:36,670 --> 00:18:38,550
But while you were worrying,

221
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:42,510
I got jealous... I'm so pathetic.

222
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:47,430
No, you're not...

223
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:49,690
I'm the same.

224
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:55,780
Every time I see you and Mabuchi-kun joking around,

225
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:59,240
it feels like you're getting ahead of me.

226
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:01,450
I get really uneasy.

227
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:10,920
I'm the one who said no hard feelings no matter who wins,

228
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:16,300
but I always get jealous, and I always feel uneasy.

229
00:19:18,170 --> 00:19:23,140
Part of the reason I didn't tell you about Mabuchi-kun's mom

230
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:29,020
was that I wanted to have a secret with him you didn't.

231
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:37,570
It hurts hearing you apologize to me like that.

232
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,490
I'm sorry.

233
00:19:47,660 --> 00:19:50,250
Doesn't this suck?

234
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:56,210
Why did we have to fall in love with the same person?

235
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,430
I've had enough!

236
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,220
Futaba-chan...

237
00:20:10,270 --> 00:20:13,940
But Yuuri, just know that I love you!

238
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:20,440
I love you too, Futaba-chan!

239
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:39,250
Let's head back.

240
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,220
Sure.

241
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:52,270
So, what's this?

242
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:57,520
A special edition of my easy-to-understand math notes.

243
00:20:57,520 --> 00:21:00,230
Take them. No need for thanks.

244
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:03,030
Aren't I just the nicest?

245
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:04,450
Take it back.

246
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:07,910
H-Hey, how hard do you think I worked to make that?

247
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,990
You're getting pretty offended for doing something I didn't ask for.

248
00:21:10,990 --> 00:21:12,370
Say that again?

249
00:21:12,370 --> 00:21:17,040
So that's how you treat favors. Oh, I see how it is.

250
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:17,040
You see?

251
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:23,050
Even when you act abrasive, that's how you show your kindness.

252
00:21:24,010 --> 00:21:27,050
I'll write you one for chemistry, too.

253
00:21:27,050 --> 00:21:29,220
Oh, that'd be great.

254
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:31,770
When are we having our next study session?

255
00:21:31,770 --> 00:21:33,680
Mabuchi-kun, when are you free?

256
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:36,560
We can even have dinner next time.

257
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:40,110
I'll whip up my specialty for you!

258
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:40,110
If Kou still feels the need to walk around at night,

259
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:44,530
then we'll just have to be the light that guides him out.

260
00:21:44,530 --> 00:21:46,070
That sounds gross.

261
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,620
I'll think about it.

262
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:05,880
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

263
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:11,260
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

264
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:16,730
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

265
00:22:16,730 --> 00:22:22,020
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

266
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:31,740
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

267
00:22:31,740 --> 00:22:37,330
but it passed, as days tend to do.

268
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:47,880
The rails carry you away

269
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:56,140
leaving me alone on our usual path.

270
00:22:57,270 --> 00:23:06,780
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

271
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:15,490
so why can't I say them?

272
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:22,460
Why can't I?

273
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:40,020
NEXT TIME...

274
00:23:29,010 --> 00:23:30,630
It's too late!

275
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:38,180
If you really feel scared, then that
